# Shell and Python context

This POSIX example writes JSON context in `sh` and consumes it from an isolated
Python process.

```sh {#shell-setup independent=true}
ctx_set greeting '"hello from sh"'
ctx_set samples '[2,4,8,16]'
printf 'Shell prepared %s\n' "$(ctx_get greeting)"
```

```python {#python-consumer depends-on=shell-setup}
ctx.total = sum(ctx.samples)
print(f"{ctx.greeting}: total={ctx.total}")
```

```python {#verify-shell role=test test-of=python-consumer}
assert ctx.greeting == "hello from sh"
assert ctx.total == 30
```
